From 3e6bb4069ac473ccc2d19b6e6b04024365542ff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bo Hu <bohu@google.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:39:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 40/42] vulkan: prevent uint32_t overflow in
 getFormatTransferInfo

getFormatTransferInfo() previously computed plane offsets, row strides,
and plane sizes using 32-bit uint32_t before assigning the result to
VkDeviceSize stagingBufferCopySize. For large ColorBuffer extents (such
as 16384x16384 with 16-bpp VK_FORMAT_R32G32B32A32_SFLOAT), planeSize
wrapped around to 0 in uint32_t while VkBufferImageCopy::imageExtent
retained the true dimensions, bypassing staging buffer size checks.

- Widen cumulativeOffset, planeOffset, planeBpp, planeStrideBytes, and
  planeSize in getFormatTransferInfo() to 64-bit VkDeviceSize, and check
  that width alignment does not overflow uint32_t.
- Template alignToPower2() and widen pixel/plane offset calculations in
  Pack/Unpack depth-stencil helpers to size_t.
- Check stagingBufferCopySize against mStaging.mAllocationSize before
  resizing/allocating host vectors in readColorBufferToBytes() and
  clearColorBuffer().
- Add unit tests in vk_format_utils_unittest.cpp covering >= 4 GiB
  single-plane and multi-plane transfer sizes and width alignment
  overflow.

Bug: 514121060
Test: bazel test //host/vulkan:vk_format_utils_tests
Change-Id: Ia327c8910ff6c97f9174ca76b2ede402e366cde5
(cherry picked from commit 2fab5a4b5763a231f457989ea8a112584e9616b3)

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#41
